    "text": "Ne sceal se bisceop him sylf n\u00e6nie abbod geceosan \u00e6fter d\u00e6s o\u00feres dea\u00f0e ne be him lifigendum, \u00feeah\nNis na to onfonne seo halige ons\u00e6gdnes of \u00f0\u00e6s m\u00e6sse preostes handa, \u00fee ne can his orationes and his\n\u00d0a \u00f0e nyton hwe\u00f0er hig gefullode beo\u00f0 and l\u00e6ta\u00f0 hy \u00e6ft fullian \u00feat bi\u00f0 swylce hig \u00e6ft crist ahon,\nGyf \u00feonne hwilc mon wene, \u00feat hit sy alyfed for sumre cl\u00e6nnesse, \u00feat hyne man tuwa fullige, \u00feonne\nBeo sunnand\u00e6ges weorce Grecas and Romana rowa\u00f0 and rida\u00f0, ac man ne mot na\u00f0er ne hlaf bacan ne\nMen ne moten ba\u00f0ian sunnan dagum, ne eac Grecas nella\u00f0 openlice writan on \u00f0am dagum, ac gif hwylc\n\u00d0a \u00f0e wyrcea\u00f0 sunnand\u00e6g \u00e6t \u00feam forman cyrre, Grecas hy ofer cida\u00f0, \u00e6t \u00feam o\u00f0rum cyrre nima\u00f0\nAnd gyf hit synt \u00feeowe men, and hig hit hyra willes do\u00f0, syn hy beswungene, and gif hit syn freo men,\nNe sceal cyrcean timber to \u00e6nigum o\u00f0rum weorce, buton to o\u00f0re cyrcean, o\u00f0\u00f0e hit man for b\u00e6rne to\nWitodlice nis \u00feat nan riht, \u00feat \u00e6nig man for geflite and for andan wi\u00f0 cwe\u00f0e godcundra hada cyre and\nCyricean man mot settan on o\u00fere stowe, gyf bit nyd \u00feearf sy, ac hy man ne mot na eft halgian, butan \u00feat\n\u00d0a neat, \u00fea beo\u00f0 gemengde to wulfum and to hundum, ne beo\u00f0 \u00fea na mannum to etanne, ac swynum\nGrecas ne sylla\u00f0 na hyra swynum astorfen fl\u00e6sc, ac hy lyfa\u00f0 \u00fea fel to sceon and \u00fea hyda and \u00fea hornas\nFugelas and o\u00f0re nytenu n\u00e6ron na lyfede to etanne, gif hi beo\u00f0 on nette awyrged, ne \u00f0eah se heafoc\n\u00d0a feower heafod cwidas in actibus apostolorum \u00feus be beoda\u00f0, \u00feat man hine forh\u00e6bbe fram dyrnum\nHors we ne forbeoda\u00f0, ac hit is ungewunelio to etanne.\nHara is alyfed to etanne and he his eac swi\u00f0e god wi\u00f0 ut sih\u00f0e, and his gealla his swi\u00f0e god wi\u00f0 pipor\nMid Grecum man moste wifigean \u00e6t \u00f0am \u00f0riddan cneowe, \u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6re ealdan \u00e6 bebode, and nonu \u00e6r \u00e6t\nAc gif hy \u00e6r \u00f0am \u00feriddan cneow hig gesamnien, \u00feonne is \u00f0\u00e6t to brecanne and nis \u00feat nanum men\nSe \u00f0e twige wifige o\u00f0\u00f0e wif ceorlige, f\u00e6ste I gear, and si\u00f0\u00f0an a wodnes dagum and frigedagum and \u00fea\n\u00deonne gif wer \u00ferywa wifa\u00f0, o\u00f0\u00f0e wif ceorla\u00f0, o\u00f0\u00f0e gyt ma, f\u00e6ste IV gear and \u00fea hwile, \u00fee he lyfige,\nGyf here genime hwylces mannes wif, and he hi ne mage eft begytan, sy \u00f0am w\u00e6re alyfed, \u00feat he\nGyf hwylc wif o\u00f0\u00f0e ceorl gehate, \u00feat hy willan on m\u00e6g\u00f0 hade \u00feurh wunian, and \u00f0onne se ceorl hine\nGyf hylces mannes wif bi\u00f0 \u00f0earnunga forlegen, \u00f0onne is him alyfed, \u00feat he forl\u00e6te hy and nime him\nNis \u00feam wife na alyfed, \u00fe\u00e6t heo forl\u00e6te hire w\u00e6r butan leafe, \u00feeah heo for beo, buton Basilius demde,\nSe \u00f0e h\u00e6me on sunnand\u00e6g, bidde him \u00e6t gode forgifnesse and f\u00e6ste III dagas.\nNis nanum men alyfed, \u00fe\u00e6t he nime on his \u00feeowe \u00e6nig feoh, butan his willan and butan forwyrhtum,\nNis \u00feam m\u00e6sse preost alyfed, \u00feat he yppe \u00fe\u00e6s bisceopes synne, far\u00f0am se bisceop h\u00e6f\u00f0 anweald ofer\nCild man mot sellan into mynstre, \u00feeah man \u00feat o\u00f0\u00e6r gehate, swa \u00f0eah is betere, \u00feat man \u00feat gehat\nEac gelice o\u00f0re nytenu man mot alysan, gif hit nyd\u00feearf bi\u00f0.\nGyf hwylc wif wiccunga bega, and \u00fea deofollican galdorsangas, blinne and f\u00e6ste an gear and \u00fea III\n\u00d0a wif, \u00f0e do\u00f0 aworpennysse hyra bearna, \u00fea ylcan gemete syn hy gedemde \u00e6r\u00f0on \u00fea bearn cwice\nAnd \u00feonne \u00e6fter \u00f0onn